# Architecture High-Level Design (C4 Model)

This document contains the System Context (Level 1) and Container (Level 2) diagrams for the National Social Insurance Platform, modeled using Mermaid.js.

## Level 1: System Context Diagram
Shows the platform and how it interacts with users and external government/banking systems.

```mermaid
C4Context
title System Context diagram for National Social Insurance Platform

Person(beneficiary, "Beneficiary", "Citizen or Resident using the platform")
Person(employer, "Employer", "Company representative managing payroll")
Person(admin, "Gov Admin", "Processes claims and monitors the system")

System(nsip, "National Social Insurance Platform", "Allows users to view benefits, employers to pay contributions, and admins to process claims.")

System_Ext(bank, "National Payment Gateway", "Processes contribution payments")
System_Ext(identity, "National Identity Service", "SSO Authentication (e.g., Absher)")
System_Ext(labor, "Ministry of Labor", "Validates employment status & contracts")

Rel(beneficiary, nsip, "Views benefits, files claims")
Rel(employer, nsip, "Uploads payroll, pays contributions")
Rel(admin, nsip, "Approves claims, views reports")

Rel(nsip, bank, "Initiates payments")
Rel(nsip, identity, "Authenticates users")
Rel(nsip, labor, "Verifies employment data")
```

## Level 2: Container Diagram
Shows the high-level microservices architecture, databases, and message brokers within the platform.

```mermaid
C4Container
title Container diagram for NSIP

Person(beneficiary, "Beneficiary")
Person(employer, "Employer")
Person(admin, "Admin")

System_Boundary(c1, "National Social Insurance Platform") {
    Container(mobile_app, "Mobile App", "Flutter", "Provides core functionality to beneficiaries.")
    Container(web_app, "Web App", "React", "Provides full functionality to employers, admins, and beneficiaries.")
    
    Container(api_gateway, "API Gateway", "Spring Cloud Gateway", "Routes requests to appropriate microservices and handles rate limiting.")
    
    Container(auth_service, "Auth Service", "Spring Boot", "Handles SSO, JWT generation.")
    Container(claim_service, "Claim Service", "Spring Boot", "Manages lifecycle of all insurance claims.")
    Container(contribution_service, "Contribution Service", "Spring Boot", "Manages employer payrolls and payments.")
    Container(notification_service, "Notification Service", "Spring Boot", "Sends SMS/Email/Push notifications.")
    
    ContainerDb(db_postgres, "Primary Database", "PostgreSQL", "Stores user data, claims, contributions.")
    ContainerDb(cache_redis, "Distributed Cache", "Redis", "Caches frequent reads (e.g. user profiles, reference data).")
    ContainerQueue(kafka, "Message Broker", "Apache Kafka", "Handles async events like 'ClaimSubmitted', 'PaymentReceived'.")
}

Rel(beneficiary, mobile_app, "Uses")
Rel(employer, web_app, "Uses")
Rel(admin, web_app, "Uses")

Rel(mobile_app, api_gateway, "Makes API calls to", "JSON/HTTPS")
Rel(web_app, api_gateway, "Makes API calls to", "JSON/HTTPS")

Rel(api_gateway, auth_service, "Routes to")
Rel(api_gateway, claim_service, "Routes to")
Rel(api_gateway, contribution_service, "Routes to")

Rel(auth_service, db_postgres, "Reads/Writes")
Rel(claim_service, db_postgres, "Reads/Writes")
Rel(contribution_service, db_postgres, "Reads/Writes")

Rel(claim_service, cache_redis, "Reads/Writes")
Rel(contribution_service, cache_redis, "Reads/Writes")

Rel(claim_service, kafka, "Publishes events to")
Rel(contribution_service, kafka, "Publishes events to")
Rel(kafka, notification_service, "Consumes events from")
```
